Z||000003||GodSend||11-06-2001||09:37 AM||||Thats a tough one, but most people I know that have had stereo's stolen get their insurance money (even if its not 100% worth) and put a new system in that is better then the old one!<P>When I had my old system stolen from my 91 Talon TSI a few years back I thought I was going to cry.  The car had everything, 2 Pheonix Gold Amps, 4 JL Audio Subs, cd Changer, in dash EQ, moterized flip down clarion deck, the works!  ALl put in by myself, took me the better part of 6 months, every weekend.<P>Anyhoots, the guys who stole it were "pretty nice" if you think about...  My interior was not touched at all (save for the hole in the dash)... The car was parked at my mechanics (where he told me he would park it inside) so my insurance company just gave me 100% worth and went after his insurance company.<P>Beauty is that they gave me 100% even for things I bought used (bought a Pheonix Gold m50 for 200$ Canadian - Replacement value was 850$ so they gave me the 850!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> - Even threw me 500$ for install "just incase you don't have time to do it again"...<P>Anyhoots, my point is, you never know what a blessing some of this stuff can be.  I could not sleep for a few days, but after that, I got a phat check for $6000 , sold the Talon for $3000 , Bought my Fiero for $8000 , put a nice alarm in it, and started on the stereo.<P>So you never know just what tomorrow may bring...<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif"> ||||reg||1
